  "issue": {
    "headline": "The largest city in Texas, and the AG rulings it asks for",
    "body": "Houston is the biggest public body in the state, and under the Public Information Act a body that wants to withhold must ask the Attorney General within ten business days and say why. Those requests and the rulings on them are themselves public. The pattern of what a city routinely asks permission to withhold is a map of what it does not want read.",
    "record": "Attorney General open-records rulings naming the City of Houston, cross-referenced against the City's own GovQA request log."
  },
